    'sun/light': { score: [1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1], seen: 'code', note: "New: act 4's room hazard (sunrise.js), a floor that hurts while you stand in it. Anticipation: the line creeps under 2 cm a second, its hard hot rim and a low hex volume over the strip it moves into next always showing in --hostile-sun. Release: stepping in, on that frame, a hiss, a puff of steam off the bell, a flash and the DRYING tag. Travel: the line itself moving across the room, lit in the room's own shaders (floor, furniture tops and sides facing the window, each surface's colour warmed, a soft edge under the hot rim). Impact: the flash and steam where the light catches the jelly. Target reaction: the bell dries (its glow fades, it goes dull and dusty) and steams, a tremor each second it bites (feel sun). Attacker reaction: the rim flares with each bite, the camera trembles. Aftermath: the bell stays dry and comes back over 2 s in the shade (the drain stops at once). Confirmation: DRYING, the Health bar, the toast the first time. Sound: the entry hiss and crackle, then a low sizzle with spits, every play pitch-varied (nothing flies, so no travel layer is owed). Proven by night4/the-sun-*." },
